A realistic legacy procedure header where declaration rules meet: a
:DECLARE before :PARAMETERS, inline initializers, a :DEFAULT on a local
after the :DECLARE, a redeclared parameter, and a local nobody uses
(strict). Each finding names a different defect in the same five lines.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ReceiveLot;
	:DECLARE nReceived := 0, sBin;
	:PARAMETERS sLotNo, nQty;
	:DEFAULT nQty, 1;
	:DEFAULT sBin, "DOCK";
	:DECLARE sLotNo, sUnused;
	nReceived := nReceived + nQty;
	sBin := "RACK-" + sLotNo;
	:RETURN {sBin, nReceived};
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ReceiveLot;
	:DECLARE nReceived := 0, sBin;
	:PARAMETERS sLotNo, nQty;
	:DEFAULT nQty, 1;
	:DEFAULT sBin, "DOCK";
	:DECLARE sLotNo, sUnused;

	nReceived := nReceived + nQty;
	sBin := "RACK-" + sLotNo;

	:RETURN {sBin, nReceived};
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
2:21-2:23 error declare_initializer: ':DECLARE' accepts only a comma-separated list of variable names - assign the value in a separate statement
3:2-3:13 error parameters_first: ':PARAMETERS' must appear immediately after ':PROCEDURE'
5:11-5:15 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'sBin' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
6:11-6:17 hint redeclare_is_noop: Variable 'sLotNo' is already declared (first declared at line 3). Re-declaration is silently ignored at runtime.
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:21-2:23 error declare_initializer: ':DECLARE' accepts only a comma-separated list of variable names - assign the value in a separate statement
3:2-3:13 error parameters_first: ':PARAMETERS' must appear immediately after ':PROCEDURE'
5:11-5:15 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'sBin' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
6:11-6:17 hint redeclare_is_noop: Variable 'sLotNo' is already declared (first declared at line 3). Re-declaration is silently ignored at runtime.
6:19-6:26 hint unused_variable: Variable 'sUnused' is declared but never used
